From d38d228f8b2832e9b08c9d0af1d22d3cd92e6486 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Russell Oliver <roliver8143@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 12:32:28 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] Bluetooth: SMP: distribute local identity for LE legacy
 OOB bonds

The kernel only offers to distribute an IRK and Identity Address when
HCI_PRIVACY is set.  Peers of the class that mandates LE legacy OOB do not
treat the bond as established until the initiator has sent Identity
Information and Identity Address Information in phase 3: without them the
peer sets its "bonded" state but keeps advertising its factory address and
never reconnects, so the pairing succeeds and is then useless.

Offer SMP_DIST_ID_KEY when a stored LE legacy OOB Temporary Key is in use.
The peer still has to request it - what gets distributed is the
intersection of the initiator's and responder's key distribution fields -
so a peer that does not ask for an IRK is unaffected.

Signed-off-by: Russell Oliver <roliver8143@gmail.com>
---
 net/bluetooth/smp.c | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/net/bluetooth/smp.c b/net/bluetooth/smp.c
index 825f6e17a..4a6f6a879 100644
--- a/net/bluetooth/smp.c
+++ b/net/bluetooth/smp.c
@@ -726,9 +726,21 @@ static void build_pairing_cmd(struct l2cap_conn *conn,
 		 * userspace supplied a Temporary Key for this peer: a peer
 		 * that mandates LE legacy OOB rejects a Pairing Request whose
 		 * OOB flag is clear.
+		 *
+		 * Offer our identity as well.  The kernel otherwise only
+		 * distributes an IRK and Identity Address under HCI_PRIVACY,
+		 * but peers of this class treat the bond as incomplete until
+		 * the initiator has sent Identity Information and Identity
+		 * Address Information in phase 3, and then never reconnect.
+		 * What is actually distributed is the intersection of the two
+		 * key distribution fields, so this only widens what we are
+		 * willing to send; a peer that does not ask for an IRK still
+		 * does not get one.
 		 */
-		if (smp_le_legacy_oob_get(hcon, NULL, NULL))
+		if (smp_le_legacy_oob_get(hcon, NULL, NULL)) {
 			oob_flag = SMP_OOB_PRESENT;
+			local_dist |= SMP_DIST_ID_KEY;
+		}
 	}
 
 	if (rsp == NULL) {
